<section class="w-full py-16 bg-white text-neutral-700 font-sans">
    <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-6 flex flex-col gap-12">
        
        <div class="flex flex-col gap-4 text-center max-w-2xl mx-auto">
            <h1 class="text-4xl/12 font-display font-black text-neutral-900 tracking-tight sm:text-5xl/14">
                Our Beliefs
            </h1>
            <p class="text-base/7 text-neutral-500 uppercase tracking-widest font-display font-bold text-primary-500">
                Free Will Baptist Core Beliefs
            </p>
            <div class="w-16 h-1 bg-primary-500 mx-auto mt-2 rounded-full"></div>
        </div>

        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-8 items-start">
            
            <!-- The Bible -->
            <div class="bg-neutral-50 border border-neutral-200 p-6 rounded-church shadow-sm flex flex-col gap-3 min-h-full">
                <h2 class="text-xl/7 font-display font-bold text-neutral-900 flex items-center gap-2">
                    <span class="w-2 h-6 bg-primary-500 rounded-full"></span>
                    The Bible
                </h2>
                <p class="text-sm/6 text-neutral-600">
                    The Scriptures of the Old and New Testaments were given by inspiration of God, and are our only infallible rule of faith and practice.
                </p>
            </div>

            <!-- God -->
            <div class="bg-neutral-50 border border-neutral-200 p-6 rounded-church shadow-sm flex flex-col gap-3 min-h-full">
                <h2 class="text-xl/7 font-display font-bold text-neutral-900 flex items-center gap-2">
                    <span class="w-2 h-6 bg-primary-500 rounded-full"></span>
                    God
                </h2>
                <p class="text-sm/6 text-neutral-600">
                    We believe that there is one God, eternally existent in three persons: the Father, Son and Holy Spirit, and that each person of the Triune Godhead is equal, eternal, and self-existent as God.
                </p>
            </div>

            <!-- Christ -->
            <div class="bg-neutral-50 border border-neutral-200 p-6 rounded-church shadow-sm flex flex-col gap-3 min-h-full">
                <h2 class="text-xl/7 font-display font-bold text-neutral-900 flex items-center gap-2">
                    <span class="w-2 h-6 bg-primary-500 rounded-full"></span>
                    Christ
                </h2>
                <p class="text-sm/6 text-neutral-600">
                    We believe in the deity of our Lord Jesus Christ, in His virgin birth, in His sinless life, in His substitutionary death, in His bodily resurrection, in His ascension to the right hand of the Father, and in His personal return in power and glory.
                </p>
            </div>

            <!-- The Holy Spirit -->
            <div class="bg-neutral-50 border border-neutral-200 p-6 rounded-church shadow-sm flex flex-col gap-3 min-h-full">
                <h2 class="text-xl/7 font-display font-bold text-neutral-900 flex items-center gap-2">
                    <span class="w-2 h-6 bg-primary-500 rounded-full"></span>
                    The Holy Spirit
                </h2>
                <p class="text-sm/6 text-neutral-600">
                    We believe in the present ministry of the Holy Spirit by whose indwelling the Christian is enabled to live a godly life.
                </p>
            </div>

            <!-- The Sinfulness of Man -->
            <div class="bg-neutral-50 border border-neutral-200 p-6 rounded-church shadow-sm flex flex-col gap-3 min-h-full">
                <h2 class="text-xl/7 font-display font-bold text-neutral-900 flex items-center gap-2">
                    <span class="w-2 h-6 bg-primary-500 rounded-full"></span>
                    The Sinfulness of Man
                </h2>
                <p class="text-sm/6 text-neutral-600">
                    Man was created innocent, but by disobedience fell into a state of sin and condemnation. All people, therefore, inherit a fallen nature of such tendencies that all who come to years of accountability, sin and become guilty before God.
                </p>
            </div>

            <!-- Salvation -->
            <div class="bg-neutral-50 border border-neutral-200 p-6 rounded-church shadow-sm flex flex-col gap-3 min-h-full">
                <h2 class="text-xl/7 font-display font-bold text-neutral-900 flex items-center gap-2">
                    <span class="w-2 h-6 bg-primary-500 rounded-full"></span>
                    Salvation
                </h2>
                <p class="text-sm/6 text-neutral-600">
                    We believe that for the salvation of lost and sinful man, regeneration by the Holy Spirit is absolutely essential. We further believe that salvation is a totally free gift from God and cannot be earned by any amount of good deeds or religious activity.
                </p>
            </div>

            <!-- Freedom of the Will -->
            <div class="bg-neutral-50 border border-neutral-200 p-6 rounded-church shadow-sm flex flex-col gap-3 min-h-full">
                <h2 class="text-xl/7 font-display font-bold text-neutral-900 flex items-center gap-2">
                    <span class="w-2 h-6 bg-primary-500 rounded-full"></span>
                    Freedom of the Will
                </h2>
                <p class="text-sm/6 text-neutral-600">
                    Under the work and influence of the Holy Spirit, the human will is freed and enabled to choose, having power to yield to the influence of the truth and the Spirit, or to resist them and perish.
                </p>
            </div>

            <!-- Eternal Future -->
            <div class="bg-neutral-50 border border-neutral-200 p-6 rounded-church shadow-sm flex flex-col gap-3 min-h-full">
                <h2 class="text-xl/7 font-display font-bold text-neutral-900 flex items-center gap-2">
                    <span class="w-2 h-6 bg-primary-500 rounded-full"></span>
                    Eternal Future
                </h2>
                <p class="text-sm/6 text-neutral-600">
                    We believe in the resurrection of both the saved and the lost; they that are saved unto the resurrection of life and they that are lost unto the resurrection of punishment.
                </p>
            </div>

        </div>

        <div class="bg-neutral-50 border border-neutral-200 p-6 sm:p-8 rounded-church shadow-sm flex flex-col gap-4">
            <h2 class="text-2xl/8 font-display font-bold text-neutral-900 flex items-center gap-3">
                <span class="size-3 bg-primary-500 rounded-full shrink-0"></span>
                The Terms of Salvation
            </h2>
            <div class="text-sm/6 text-neutral-600 flex flex-col gap-4">
                <p>The conditions of salvation are:</p>
                <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-6">
                    <div class="bg-white p-5 border border-neutral-200 rounded-sm">
                        <span class="text-xs font-display font-black text-primary-500 uppercase tracking-wider block mb-1">Condition 1</span>
                        <strong class="text-neutral-900 block mb-2 text-base/5">Repentance of sin</strong>
                        Sincere sorrow for sin and hearty renunciation of it.
                    </div>
                    <div class="bg-white p-5 border border-neutral-200 rounded-sm">
                        <span class="text-xs font-display font-black text-primary-500 uppercase tracking-wider block mb-1">Condition 2</span>
                        <strong class="text-neutral-900 block mb-2 text-base/5">Faith in Christ</strong>
                        The unreserved committal of one’s self to Christ as Savior and Lord with purpose to love and obey Him in all things.
                    </div>
                    <div class="bg-white p-5 border border-neutral-200 rounded-sm">
                        <span class="text-xs font-display font-black text-primary-500 uppercase tracking-wider block mb-1">Condition 3</span>
                        <strong class="text-neutral-900 block mb-2 text-base/5">Continuance</strong>
                        Continuance in faith unto death.
                    </div>
                </div>
                <p class="mt-2 pt-4 border-t border-neutral-200 italic text-neutral-500">
                    Repentance and faith are not to be viewed as two separate actions, but two ways of stating the same decision. In the exercise of saving faith, the soul is renewed by the Holy Spirit, freed from the dominion of sin, and becomes a child of God.
                </p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="bg-neutral-50 border border-neutral-200 p-6 sm:p-8 rounded-church shadow-sm flex flex-col gap-3">
            <h2 class="text-xl/7 font-display font-bold text-neutral-900 flex items-center gap-2">
                <span class="w-2 h-6 bg-primary-500 rounded-full"></span>
                The Church
            </h2>
            <p class="text-sm/6 text-neutral-600">
                We believe in the spiritual unity of believers in our Lord Jesus Christ. Northwest recognizes that we are one gathering of believers who make up just one part of the universal body of Christ, the Church. We share Christian fellowship with all who hold Jesus as their one and only Savior.
            </p>
        </div>

        <hr class="border-t border-neutral-200 my-4">

        <div class="bg-linear-to-br from-neutral-900 to-neutral-800 text-white p-8 rounded-church shadow-md text-center flex flex-col gap-6 items-center max-w-3xl mx-auto w-full">
            <div class="flex flex-col gap-2">
                <h3 class="text-2xl/8 font-display font-black tracking-tight">
                    Want to know more?
                </h3>
                <p class="text-neutral-300 text-sm/6 max-w-xl">
                    Attend our services, ask questions, and check us out. Don't hesitate to ask about our <span class="text-white font-semibold">Intro to Northwest</span> class frequently offered right here at the church.
                </p>
            </div>
            <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row gap-4 items-center justify-center w-full mt-2">
                <a href="mailto:office@northwestcommunity.net" 
                   class="inline-flex items-center justify-center bg-primary-500 text-white font-display font-bold px-6 py-3 rounded-church hover:bg-primary-600 transition-colors shadow-xs text-sm">
                    <svg class="size-4 mr-2 fill-current" viewBox="0 0 20 20">
                        <path d="M2.003 5.884L10 9.882l7.997-3.998A2 2 0 0016 4H4a2 2 0 00-1.997 1.884z"/>
                        <path d="M18 8.118l-8 4-8-4V14a2 2 0 002 2h12a2 2 0 002-2V8.118z"/>
                    </svg>
                    E-mail us at office@northwestcommunity.net
                </a>
            </div>
        </div>

    </div>
</section>

<section class="w-full py-16 bg-white text-neutral-700 font-sans">
    <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-6 flex flex-col gap-12">
        
        <div class="flex flex-col gap-4 text-center max-w-2xl mx-auto">
            <h1 class="text-4xl/12 font-display font-black text-neutral-900 tracking-tight sm:text-5xl/14">
                Nuestras Creencias
            </h1>
            <p class="text-base/7 text-neutral-500 uppercase tracking-widest font-display font-bold text-primary-500">
                Creencias Básicas de FWB
            </p>
            <div class="w-16 h-1 bg-primary-500 mx-auto mt-2 rounded-full"></div>
        </div>

        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-8 items-start">
            
            <!-- La Biblia -->
            <div class="bg-neutral-50 border border-neutral-200 p-6 rounded-church shadow-sm flex flex-col gap-3 min-h-full">
                <h2 class="text-xl/7 font-display font-bold text-neutral-900 flex items-center gap-2">
                    <span class="w-2 h-6 bg-primary-500 rounded-full"></span>
                    La Biblia
                </h2>
                <p class="text-sm/6 text-neutral-600">
                    Las Escrituras del Antiguo y Nuevo Testamento fueron dadas por inspiración de Dios, y son nuestra única regla infalible de fe y práctica.
                </p>
            </div>

            <!-- Dios -->
            <div class="bg-neutral-50 border border-neutral-200 p-6 rounded-church shadow-sm flex flex-col gap-3 min-h-full">
                <h2 class="text-xl/7 font-display font-bold text-neutral-900 flex items-center gap-2">
                    <span class="w-2 h-6 bg-primary-500 rounded-full"></span>
                    Dios
                </h2>
                <p class="text-sm/6 text-neutral-600">
                    Creemos que hay un Dios, eternamente existent en tres personas: el Padre, el Hijo y el Espíritu Santo, y que cada persona de la Trinidad Triuna es igual, eterna y autoexistente como Dios.
                </p>
            </div>

            <!-- Cristo -->
            <div class="bg-neutral-50 border border-neutral-200 p-6 rounded-church shadow-sm flex flex-col gap-3 min-h-full">
                <h2 class="text-xl/7 font-display font-bold text-neutral-900 flex items-center gap-2">
                    <span class="w-2 h-6 bg-primary-500 rounded-full"></span>
                    Cristo
                </h2>
                <p class="text-sm/6 text-neutral-600">
                    Creemos en la deidad de nuestro Señor Jesucristo, en su nacimiento virginal, en su vida sin pecado, en su muerte sustitutiva, en su resurrección corporal, en su ascensión a la diestra del Padre, y en su retorno personal en poder y gloria.
                </p>
            </div>

            <!-- El Espíritu Santo -->
            <div class="bg-neutral-50 border border-neutral-200 p-6 rounded-church shadow-sm flex flex-col gap-3 min-h-full">
                <h2 class="text-xl/7 font-display font-bold text-neutral-900 flex items-center gap-2">
                    <span class="w-2 h-6 bg-primary-500 rounded-full"></span>
                    El Espíritu Santo
                </h2>
                <p class="text-sm/6 text-neutral-600">
                    Creemos en el ministerio actual del Espíritu Santo por medio del cual el cristiano puede vivir una vida santa.
                </p>
            </div>

            <!-- La Pecaminosidad del Hombre -->
            <div class="bg-neutral-50 border border-neutral-200 p-6 rounded-church shadow-sm flex flex-col gap-3 min-h-full">
                <h2 class="text-xl/7 font-display font-bold text-neutral-900 flex items-center gap-2">
                    <span class="w-2 h-6 bg-primary-500 rounded-full"></span>
                    La Pecaminosidad del Hombre
                </h2>
                <p class="text-sm/6 text-neutral-600">
                    El hombre fue creado inocente, pero por desobediencia cayó en un estado de pecado y condena. Todas las personas, por lo tanto, heredan una naturaleza caída de tales tendencias que todos los que llegan a años de responsabilidad, pesan y se vuelven culpables ante Dios.
                </p>
            </div>

            <!-- Salvación -->
            <div class="bg-neutral-50 border border-neutral-200 p-6 rounded-church shadow-sm flex flex-col gap-3 min-h-full">
                <h2 class="text-xl/7 font-display font-bold text-neutral-900 flex items-center gap-2">
                    <span class="w-2 h-6 bg-primary-500 rounded-full"></span>
                    Salvación
                </h2>
                <p class="text-sm/6 text-neutral-600">
                    Creemos que para la salvación del hombre perdido y pecador, la regeneración por el Espíritu Santo es absolutamente esencial. Además, creemos que la salvación es un regalo totalmente gratuito de Dios y no puede ganarse con cualquier cantidad de buenas obras o actividades religiosas.
                </p>
            </div>

            <!-- Libertad de la Voluntad -->
            <div class="bg-neutral-50 border border-neutral-200 p-6 rounded-church shadow-sm flex flex-col gap-3 min-h-full">
                <h2 class="text-xl/7 font-display font-bold text-neutral-900 flex items-center gap-2">
                    <span class="w-2 h-6 bg-primary-500 rounded-full"></span>
                    Libertad de la Voluntad
                </h2>
                <p class="text-sm/6 text-neutral-600">
                    Bajo la obra e influencia del Espíritu Santo, la voluntad humana es liberada y habilitada para elegir, tener poder para ceder a la influencia de la verdad y el Espíritu, o resistirlos y perecer.
                </p>
            </div>

            <!-- Futuro Eterno -->
            <div class="bg-neutral-50 border border-neutral-200 p-6 rounded-church shadow-sm flex flex-col gap-3 min-h-full">
                <h2 class="text-xl/7 font-display font-bold text-neutral-900 flex items-center gap-2">
                    <span class="w-2 h-6 bg-primary-500 rounded-full"></span>
                    Futuro Eterno
                </h2>
                <p class="text-sm/6 text-neutral-600">
                    Creemos en la resurrección de los salvados y los perdidos; los que se salvan para la resurrección de la vida y los que se pierden para la resurrección del castigo.
                </p>
            </div>

        </div>

        <div class="bg-neutral-50 border border-neutral-200 p-6 sm:p-8 rounded-church shadow-sm flex flex-col gap-4">
            <h2 class="text-2xl/8 font-display font-bold text-neutral-900 flex items-center gap-3">
                <span class="size-3 bg-primary-500 rounded-full shrink-0"></span>
                Los Términos de la Salvación
            </h2>
            <div class="text-sm/6 text-neutral-600 flex flex-col gap-4">
                <p>Las condiciones de salvación son:</p>
                <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-6">
                    <div class="bg-white p-5 border border-neutral-200 rounded-sm">
                        <span class="text-xs font-display font-black text-primary-500 uppercase tracking-wider block mb-1">Condición 1</span>
                        <strong class="text-neutral-900 block mb-2 text-base/5">Arrepentimiento</strong>
                        Arrepentimiento del pecado o sincero dolor por el pecado y renuncia sincera al mismo.
                    </div>
                    <div class="bg-white p-5 border border-neutral-200 rounded-sm">
                        <span class="text-xs font-display font-black text-primary-500 uppercase tracking-wider block mb-1">Condición 2</span>
                        <strong class="text-neutral-900 block mb-2 text-base/5">Fe</strong>
                        La fe o el compromiso incondicional de uno mismo con Cristo como Salvador y Señor con el propósito de amarlo y obedecerlo en todas las cosas.
                    </div>
                    <div class="bg-white p-5 border border-neutral-200 rounded-sm">
                        <span class="text-xs font-display font-black text-primary-500 uppercase tracking-wider block mb-1">Condición 3</span>
                        <strong class="text-neutral-900 block mb-2 text-base/5">Continuación</strong>
                        Continuación en la fe hasta la muerte.
                    </div>
                </div>
                <p class="mt-2 pt-4 border-t border-neutral-200 italic text-neutral-500">
                    El arrepentimiento y la fe no deben ser vistos como dos acciones separadas, sino dos formas de declarar la misma decisión. En el ejercicio de la fe salvadora, el alma es renovada por el Espíritu Santo, liberada del dominio del pecado, y se convierte en un hijo de Dios.
                </p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="bg-neutral-50 border border-neutral-200 p-6 sm:p-8 rounded-church shadow-sm flex flex-col gap-3">
            <h2 class="text-xl/7 font-display font-bold text-neutral-900 flex items-center gap-2">
                <span class="w-2 h-6 bg-primary-500 rounded-full"></span>
                La Iglesia
            </h2>
            <p class="text-sm/6 text-neutral-600">
                Creemos en la unidad espiritual de los creyentes en nuestro Señor Jesucristo. Northwest reconoce que somos una reunión de creyentes que constituyen solo una parte del cuerpo universal de Cristo, la Iglesia. Compartimos la comunión cristiana con todos los que tienen a Jesús como su único y único Salvador.
            </p>
        </div>

        <hr class="border-t border-neutral-200 my-4">

        <div class="bg-linear-to-br from-neutral-900 to-neutral-800 text-white p-8 rounded-church shadow-md text-center flex flex-col gap-6 items-center max-w-3xl mx-auto w-full">
            <div class="flex flex-col gap-2">
                <h3 class="text-2xl/8 font-display font-black tracking-tight">
                    ¿Quiere saber más?
                </h3>
                <p class="text-neutral-300 text-sm/6 max-w-xl">
                    Asista a nuestros servicios, haga preguntas y visítenos. No dude en preguntar por nuestra clase de <span class="text-white font-semibold">Introducción al Noroeste</span> que se ofrece con frecuencia en nuestra iglesia.
                </p>
            </div>
            <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row gap-4 items-center justify-center w-full mt-2">
                <a href="mailto:office@northwestcommunity.net" 
                   class="inline-flex items-center justify-center bg-primary-500 text-white font-display font-bold px-6 py-3 rounded-church hover:bg-primary-600 transition-colors shadow-xs text-sm">
                    <svg class="size-4 mr-2 fill-current" viewBox="0 0 20 20">
                        <path d="M2.003 5.884L10 9.882l7.997-3.998A2 2 0 0016 4H4a2 2 0 00-1.997 1.884z"/>
                        <path d="M18 8.118l-8 4-8-4V14a2 2 0 002 2h12a2 2 0 002-2V8.118z"/>
                    </svg>
                    Envíenos un correo electrónico a office@northwestcommunity.net
                </a>
            </div>
        </div>

    </div>
</section>